# RGSP only: physical observations in RGSP_INPUT_CALIBRATION_20260906.md.
# Generic.kcm supplies unhandled BUTTON_A/B -> confirm/back fallbacks.
# Lock-screen bring-up policy: physical A must be a direct confirm/unlock.
key 304 ENTER
key 305 BUTTON_B
key 307 BUTTON_X
key 306 BUTTON_Y
key 308 BUTTON_L1
key 309 BUTTON_R1
key 314 BUTTON_L2
key 315 BUTTON_R2
key 310 BUTTON_SELECT
key 311 BUTTON_START
key 312 BUTTON_MODE
key 317 BUTTON_THUMBL
key 318 BUTTON_THUMBR
key 114 VOLUME_DOWN
key 115 VOLUME_UP

# Menu's extra release-time 0x162 pulse is deliberately unmapped.
# BUTTON_MODE falls back to HOME; do not also dispatch the extra pulse.
# Optional RG34XXSP add-on exposes these four unused Linux axes. The original
# RX/RY/RZ ternary BSP signals remain unassigned, preserving old-model input.
axis 0x00 X
axis 0x01 Y
axis 0x02 Z
axis 0x07 RZ
axis 0x10 HAT_X
axis 0x11 HAT_Y
